// computation kernel
//
// Optimizations compared to the original kernel:
//  - Use traversal orders that follow the physical layouts chosen in `tuning`
//    so that the innermost loops walk contiguous memory in both inputs and outputs.
//  - Accumulate using scalar temporaries (a_ik, c_jm, e_ij) to avoid reloading
//    the same matrix elements for each innermost‑loop iteration.
//  - Initialize E, F, and G once before their respective accumulation loops
//    instead of re‑initializing inside the reduction loops.
